 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Schott et al. in 2013 [S1]. It extends the Directional Occlusion Shading (DOS) model, previously presented by Schott et al. [24], to include geometric primitives [S1]. The approach builds on incremental filtering techniques used for volumetric scattering [S1]. It addresses limitations in screen-space ambient occlusion methods that approximate low-frequency occlusion with spheres or use summed area tables for global occlusion [S1].
